wayland-client: Connection::connect_to_env() on Haiku

Haiku's libwayland-client talks to an in-process server (wayland-server-inproc.so) that
wl_display_connect() sets up; there are no Wayland sockets, so WAYLAND_SOCKET, WAYLAND_DISPLAY and
XDG_RUNTIME_DIR mean nothing there. On Haiku connect_to_env() uses wayland-backend's
connect_default() (the wayland-backend patch) instead. Needs the "system" feature (winit enables
it). Applies with -p1 to wayland-client 0.31.15.

--- a/src/conn.rs
+++ b/src/conn.rs
@@ -43,6 +43,20 @@
